{
 "lesson": 25,
 "duration": 740.501625,
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.59,
   "end": 3.59,
   "text": "What was to live, like to live somewhere?"
  },
  {
   "start": 5.59,
   "end": 13.59,
   "text": "Habite, habite, h-a-b-i-t-e-a, habite, school is école."
  },
  {
   "start": 13.59,
   "end": 16.97,
   "text": "How would you say the school?"
  },
  {
   "start": 16.97,
   "end": 17.97,
   "text": "L'école."
  },
  {
   "start": 17.97,
   "end": 27.97,
   "text": "L'école, so we don't know what gender it is yet, but we do know how to say the school because le hola will just contract with école."
  },
  {
   "start": 27.97,
   "end": 33.97,
   "text": "But école is spelled e-c-o-l-e, so what gender do you think it is?"
  },
  {
   "start": 34.97,
   "end": 36.97,
   "text": "La, feminine."
  },
  {
   "start": 36.97,
   "end": 45.97,
   "text": "Feminine, good, no? We have the final e ending, so it's most probably feminine and it is la école becoming l'école."
  },
  {
   "start": 45.97,
   "end": 54.97,
   "text": "Près de means near to, près de, like present, près is spelled p-r-e-s, près."
  },
  {
   "start": 54.97,
   "end": 60.97,
   "text": "So près de means near to, how would you say near to the school?"
  },
  {
   "start": 61.97,
   "end": 65.97,
   "text": "Près de l'école."
  },
  {
   "start": 65.97,
   "end": 72.97,
   "text": "Very good, so we're not actually saying near to now, but near from, near of, près de l'école."
  },
  {
   "start": 72.97,
   "end": 75.97,
   "text": "I live close to the school."
  },
  {
   "start": 75.97,
   "end": 81.34,
   "text": "Habite, près de l'école."
  },
  {
   "start": 81.34,
   "end": 85.34,
   "text": "Very good, habite, près de l'école."
  },
  {
   "start": 85.34,
   "end": 94.34,
   "text": "So we have a lot of different e's here, près is our biggest most open e in French, près de l'école."
  },
  {
   "start": 94.34,
   "end": 102.34,
   "text": "Hospital in French is hôpital, h-o-p-i-t-a-l."
  },
  {
   "start": 102.34,
   "end": 111.34,
   "text": "So we have the silent h again, like in habite and there's no s here, hôpital, hôpital."
  },
  {
   "start": 111.34,
   "end": 117.34,
   "text": "How would you say he lives near to close by the hospital?"
  },
  {
   "start": 117.34,
   "end": 123.34,
   "text": "Il habite près de l'hôpital."
  },
  {
   "start": 123.34,
   "end": 127.34,
   "text": "Il habite près de l'hôpital."
  },
  {
   "start": 127.34,
   "end": 130.34,
   "text": "Il habite près de l'hôpital."
  },
  {
   "start": 130.34,
   "end": 132.34,
   "text": "What was the word for e's?"
  },
  {
   "start": 132.34,
   "end": 135.34,
   "text": "Like in she is, he is."
  },
  {
   "start": 135.34,
   "end": 139.66,
   "text": "Eh, eh, good, spelled est, eh."
  },
  {
   "start": 139.66,
   "end": 142.66,
   "text": "So school was école."
  },
  {
   "start": 142.66,
   "end": 146.66,
   "text": "How would you say she is close by the school?"
  },
  {
   "start": 146.66,
   "end": 150.66,
   "text": "Elle est près de l'école."
  },
  {
   "start": 150.66,
   "end": 155.66,
   "text": "Very good, elle est près de l'école."
  },
  {
   "start": 155.66,
   "end": 162.66,
   "text": "So school, école and hospital, hôpital actually reveal a pattern to us."
  },
  {
   "start": 162.66,
   "end": 165.66,
   "text": "Quite an odd and interesting one."
  },
  {
   "start": 165.66,
   "end": 172.66,
   "text": "When we have s-p, s-t, s plus a hard sound basically, like p-t-q,"
  },
  {
   "start": 172.66,
   "end": 178.66,
   "text": "in a word that's the same in French and English, the s disappears in French."
  },
  {
   "start": 178.66,
   "end": 184.66,
   "text": "And in fact we've already seen this, what was the word for party in French party?"
  },
  {
   "start": 184.66,
   "end": 186.66,
   "text": "Fait."
  },
  {
   "start": 186.66,
   "end": 190.66,
   "text": "Fait, and this was feast festival, no?"
  },
  {
   "start": 190.66,
   "end": 197.66,
   "text": "The s of feast festival before that hard t disappears in the French word and we got fait."
  },
  {
   "start": 197.66,
   "end": 202.66,
   "text": "It's also the same pattern that we see between monster and montrer."
  },
  {
   "start": 202.66,
   "end": 208.66,
   "text": "There we have the s disappearing before that t, monster montrer to show,"
  },
  {
   "start": 208.66,
   "end": 213.66,
   "text": "which we saw was coming from monster related to the meaning of hormones."
  },
  {
   "start": 213.66,
   "end": 218.66,
   "text": "And when that s does leave, it also leaves an accent"
  },
  {
   "start": 218.66,
   "end": 223.66,
   "text": "on the preceding vowel to make sure everybody knows it was there, usually."
  },
  {
   "start": 223.66,
   "end": 228.66,
   "text": "And that's the little hat, the little circumflex I mentioned in fait."
  },
  {
   "start": 228.66,
   "end": 232.66,
   "text": "And we also have it on the o of hôpital, for example."
  },
  {
   "start": 232.66,
   "end": 234.66,
   "text": "And this is quite a common pattern."
  },
  {
   "start": 234.66,
   "end": 238.66,
   "text": "For example, the word forest in French is the same,"
  },
  {
   "start": 238.66,
   "end": 243.66,
   "text": "but just without that s coming before that hard t."
  },
  {
   "start": 243.66,
   "end": 247.66,
   "text": "So how would that sound in French, forest?"
  },
  {
   "start": 247.66,
   "end": 248.66,
   "text": "Forest."
  },
  {
   "start": 248.66,
   "end": 250.66,
   "text": "Good, but would you pronounce that last t?"
  },
  {
   "start": 250.66,
   "end": 251.66,
   "text": "Forest."
  },
  {
   "start": 251.66,
   "end": 253.66,
   "text": "Forest, very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 253.66,
   "end": 254.66,
   "text": "La forêt."
  },
  {
   "start": 254.66,
   "end": 257.66,
   "text": "How would you say I'm close by the forest?"
  },
  {
   "start": 257.66,
   "end": 260.66,
   "text": "I'm close by the forest, I'm near the forest."
  },
  {
   "start": 260.66,
   "end": 266.66,
   "text": "Je suis près de la forêt."
  },
  {
   "start": 266.66,
   "end": 267.66,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 267.66,
   "end": 270.66,
   "text": "Je suis près de la forêt."
  },
  {
   "start": 270.66,
   "end": 271.66,
   "text": "Beast."
  },
  {
   "start": 271.66,
   "end": 275.66,
   "text": "The beast in French is la bête, la bête."
  },
  {
   "start": 275.66,
   "end": 276.66,
   "text": "La bête."
  },
  {
   "start": 276.66,
   "end": 281.66,
   "text": "This is b-e-t-e, which is, of course, why we hear the t, la bête."
  },
  {
   "start": 281.66,
   "end": 283.66,
   "text": "Interest."
  },
  {
   "start": 283.66,
   "end": 285.66,
   "text": "How might that sound in French?"
  },
  {
   "start": 285.66,
   "end": 288.66,
   "text": "Interest is in the interest."
  },
  {
   "start": 288.66,
   "end": 289.66,
   "text": "Interest."
  },
  {
   "start": 289.66,
   "end": 290.66,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 290.66,
   "end": 296.66,
   "text": "But we have the i-n syllable, non, I can envite."
  },
  {
   "start": 296.66,
   "end": 297.66,
   "text": "Antere."
  },
  {
   "start": 297.66,
   "end": 298.66,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 298.66,
   "end": 302.66,
   "text": "Antere, l'antere, which is actually le, it's masculine."
  },
  {
   "start": 302.66,
   "end": 303.66,
   "text": "L'antere."
  },
  {
   "start": 303.66,
   "end": 310.66,
   "text": "We could have la cote, the cote, le coup."
  },
  {
   "start": 310.66,
   "end": 312.66,
   "text": "C-o-u-t, the cote."
  },
  {
   "start": 312.66,
   "end": 317.66,
   "text": "We could have la pâte, the paste or pastry."
  },
  {
   "start": 317.66,
   "end": 321.66,
   "text": "And in the plural, p-a-t-e-s, pasta."
  },
  {
   "start": 321.66,
   "end": 324.66,
   "text": "It means pasta, le pâte."
  },
  {
   "start": 324.66,
   "end": 327.97,
   "text": "He is eating the pasta."
  },
  {
   "start": 327.97,
   "end": 330.97,
   "text": "Il mange la pâte."
  },
  {
   "start": 330.97,
   "end": 332.97,
   "text": "In plural to get the meaning of pasta."
  },
  {
   "start": 332.97,
   "end": 334.97,
   "text": "We put it in plural."
  },
  {
   "start": 334.97,
   "end": 336.97,
   "text": "Le, le, pâte."
  },
  {
   "start": 336.97,
   "end": 337.97,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 337.97,
   "end": 340.97,
   "text": "Il mange la pâte."
  },
  {
   "start": 340.97,
   "end": 343.97,
   "text": "Even the word crepe is also from this pattern."
  },
  {
   "start": 343.97,
   "end": 347.97,
   "text": "We have crisp or crispy in English."
  },
  {
   "start": 347.97,
   "end": 350.97,
   "text": "No, crepe is the same root as crisp,"
  },
  {
   "start": 350.97,
   "end": 354.97,
   "text": "but with the s again before that hard p-sound disappears."
  },
  {
   "start": 354.97,
   "end": 358.97,
   "text": "Island or isle in French is spelled isle."
  },
  {
   "start": 358.97,
   "end": 360.97,
   "text": "How would that sound?"
  },
  {
   "start": 360.97,
   "end": 361.97,
   "text": "Il."
  },
  {
   "start": 361.97,
   "end": 362.97,
   "text": "Il."
  },
  {
   "start": 362.97,
   "end": 363.97,
   "text": "Il."
  },
  {
   "start": 363.97,
   "end": 364.97,
   "text": "The same as he."
  },
  {
   "start": 364.97,
   "end": 367.97,
   "text": "The word for storm, tampit."
  },
  {
   "start": 367.97,
   "end": 371.97,
   "text": "You might not realise that this is just tempest, tampit."
  },
  {
   "start": 371.97,
   "end": 375.97,
   "text": "So there's many a word with this pattern of an S"
  },
  {
   "start": 375.97,
   "end": 381.97,
   "text": "in the S-T-S-P-S-C combination disappearing in the French word."
  },
  {
   "start": 381.97,
   "end": 383.97,
   "text": "And this means we have yet another curious way"
  },
  {
   "start": 383.97,
   "end": 387.97,
   "text": "to internalise the vocabulary that we come across"
  },
  {
   "start": 387.97,
   "end": 390.97,
   "text": "in finding examples of this pattern."
  },
  {
   "start": 390.97,
   "end": 394.97,
   "text": "To stop in French is arrêter, arrêter."
  },
  {
   "start": 394.97,
   "end": 395.97,
   "text": "To stop."
  },
  {
   "start": 395.97,
   "end": 396.97,
   "text": "Arrêter."
  },
  {
   "start": 396.97,
   "end": 401.97,
   "text": "That's spelled A-R-A-I with a little hat on it."
  },
  {
   "start": 401.97,
   "end": 403.97,
   "text": "T-E-R."
  },
  {
   "start": 403.97,
   "end": 407.97,
   "text": "What might it be connected to in English?"
  },
  {
   "start": 407.97,
   "end": 412.97,
   "text": "A-R-R-E with the little hat T and then the verb ending E-R."
  },
  {
   "start": 412.97,
   "end": 415.38,
   "text": "Arrest."
  },
  {
   "start": 415.38,
   "end": 416.38,
   "text": "To arrest."
  },
  {
   "start": 416.38,
   "end": 417.38,
   "text": "Good, no?"
  },
  {
   "start": 417.38,
   "end": 420.38,
   "text": "And it also means to arrest in French."
  },
  {
   "start": 420.38,
   "end": 423.38,
   "text": "But also for the common meaning of to stop."
  },
  {
   "start": 423.38,
   "end": 424.38,
   "text": "Arrêter."
  },
  {
   "start": 424.38,
   "end": 428.38,
   "text": "How would you say I'm stopping the car?"
  },
  {
   "start": 428.38,
   "end": 432.38,
   "text": "Je, j'arrête, la voiture."
  },
  {
   "start": 432.38,
   "end": 433.38,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 433.38,
   "end": 435.38,
   "text": "J'arrête, la voiture."
  },
  {
   "start": 435.38,
   "end": 438.38,
   "text": "Now also we have arrêter, to stop."
  },
  {
   "start": 438.38,
   "end": 441.38,
   "text": "We don't pronounce that ending to get the I form."
  },
  {
   "start": 441.38,
   "end": 442.38,
   "text": "Je, arrête."
  },
  {
   "start": 442.38,
   "end": 444.38,
   "text": "And of course that contracts."
  },
  {
   "start": 444.38,
   "end": 445.38,
   "text": "J'arrête."
  },
  {
   "start": 445.38,
   "end": 447.38,
   "text": "J'arrête, la voiture."
  },
  {
   "start": 447.38,
   "end": 449.38,
   "text": "He's stopping the car."
  },
  {
   "start": 449.38,
   "end": 451.38,
   "text": "He's stopping the car."
  },
  {
   "start": 451.38,
   "end": 454.38,
   "text": "Il, arrête, la voiture."
  },
  {
   "start": 454.38,
   "end": 455.38,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 455.38,
   "end": 458.38,
   "text": "Il, arrête, la voiture."
  },
  {
   "start": 458.38,
   "end": 459.38,
   "text": "Fume."
  },
  {
   "start": 459.38,
   "end": 464.38,
   "text": "Fume in English comes from the word smoke in French."
  },
  {
   "start": 464.38,
   "end": 466.38,
   "text": "And to smoke is fume."
  },
  {
   "start": 466.38,
   "end": 468.38,
   "text": "F-U-M-I-A."
  },
  {
   "start": 468.38,
   "end": 469.38,
   "text": "Fume."
  },
  {
   "start": 469.38,
   "end": 470.38,
   "text": "Fume."
  },
  {
   "start": 470.38,
   "end": 471.38,
   "text": "Fume."
  },
  {
   "start": 471.38,
   "end": 476.38,
   "text": "If you want to say I want to stop, I want to quit smoking."
  },
  {
   "start": 476.38,
   "end": 481.38,
   "text": "In French you can say I want to stop off smoking, off to smoke."
  },
  {
   "start": 481.38,
   "end": 486.38,
   "text": "So I want to stop off to smoke."
  },
  {
   "start": 486.38,
   "end": 489.38,
   "text": "Je, vais, arrête."
  },
  {
   "start": 489.38,
   "end": 492.38,
   "text": "Arrêter, de, fumer."
  },
  {
   "start": 492.38,
   "end": 496.38,
   "text": "Je, veux, arrête, de, fumer."
  },
  {
   "start": 496.38,
   "end": 499.38,
   "text": "So arrêter, en, arrête, de."
  },
  {
   "start": 499.38,
   "end": 501.38,
   "text": "Also means to quit."
  },
  {
   "start": 501.38,
   "end": 504.38,
   "text": "How would you say I'm stopping smoking?"
  },
  {
   "start": 504.38,
   "end": 507.38,
   "text": "I'm quitting smoking rather than I want to stop smoking,"
  },
  {
   "start": 507.38,
   "end": 510.38,
   "text": "just I'm quitting smoking."
  },
  {
   "start": 510.38,
   "end": 513.38,
   "text": "J'arrête, de, fumer."
  },
  {
   "start": 513.38,
   "end": 514.38,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 514.38,
   "end": 516.38,
   "text": "J'arrête, de, fumer."
  },
  {
   "start": 516.38,
   "end": 521.38,
   "text": "If you want to say I'm stopping, not saying what you're stopping,"
  },
  {
   "start": 521.38,
   "end": 525.38,
   "text": "just I'm stopping, then what you mean in French at least,"
  },
  {
   "start": 525.38,
   "end": 527.38,
   "text": "is I'm stopping myself."
  },
  {
   "start": 527.38,
   "end": 529.38,
   "text": "I'm stopping myself."
  },
  {
   "start": 529.38,
   "end": 530.38,
   "text": "So how would that be?"
  },
  {
   "start": 530.38,
   "end": 532.38,
   "text": "I'm stopping."
  },
  {
   "start": 532.38,
   "end": 535.38,
   "text": "Je, m'arrête."
  },
  {
   "start": 535.38,
   "end": 536.38,
   "text": "Je, m'arrête."
  },
  {
   "start": 536.38,
   "end": 540.38,
   "text": "So without contractions it would be je, me, arrête, non?"
  },
  {
   "start": 540.38,
   "end": 543.38,
   "text": "And when we put that together, je, m'arrête."
  },
  {
   "start": 543.38,
   "end": 547.38,
   "text": "I don't stop, I'm not stopping."
  },
  {
   "start": 547.38,
   "end": 551.38,
   "text": "Je, ne, m'arrête pas."
  },
  {
   "start": 551.38,
   "end": 552.38,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 552.38,
   "end": 554.38,
   "text": "Je, ne, m'arrête pas."
  },
  {
   "start": 554.38,
   "end": 556.38,
   "text": "Or just je, m'arrête pas."
  },
  {
   "start": 556.38,
   "end": 557.38,
   "text": "You, stop."
  },
  {
   "start": 557.38,
   "end": 560.88,
   "text": "Tu, t'arrêtes."
  },
  {
   "start": 560.88,
   "end": 561.88,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 561.88,
   "end": 562.88,
   "text": "Tu, t'arrêtes."
  },
  {
   "start": 562.88,
   "end": 566.88,
   "text": "Of course if we need to say je, me, arrêtes, non?"
  },
  {
   "start": 566.88,
   "end": 567.88,
   "text": "Je m'arrête."
  },
  {
   "start": 567.88,
   "end": 568.88,
   "text": "I stop myself."
  },
  {
   "start": 568.88,
   "end": 569.88,
   "text": "You stop it."
  },
  {
   "start": 569.88,
   "end": 570.88,
   "text": "You stop yourself."
  },
  {
   "start": 570.88,
   "end": 572.88,
   "text": "Tu, t'arrêtes."
  },
  {
   "start": 572.88,
   "end": 574.88,
   "text": "Don't you stop."
  },
  {
   "start": 574.88,
   "end": 575.88,
   "text": "Aren't you stopping?"
  },
  {
   "start": 575.88,
   "end": 578.88,
   "text": "You don't stop."
  },
  {
   "start": 578.88,
   "end": 582.88,
   "text": "Tu, tu, ne, t'arrêtes pas."
  },
  {
   "start": 582.88,
   "end": 583.88,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 583.88,
   "end": 586.88,
